# Sovereign Twilio & SMS Router — LOCKDOWN

The Twilio integration and Sovereign SMS Router are A2P compliance infrastructure. A single mistake here causes carrier filtering, TCPA violations, or financial liability.

## Protected Files — READ ONLY

- `server/routes/twilioWebhooks.ts` — inbound SMS/Voice webhook receiver
- `server/services/smsRouter.ts` — Sovereign SMS Router (6-pipe intent dispatch)
- `server/twilio.ts` — Twilio client initialization
- `server/taskScheduler.ts` — 24-hour SMS automation scheduler
- `migrations/0010_sms_compliance_router.sql`
- `migrations/0011_compliance_reseller_gateway.sql`

## Absolute Prohibitions

- NEVER bypass `validateTwilioSignature()`. Every inbound webhook MUST be HMAC-validated.
- NEVER hardcode Twilio Account SIDs, Auth Tokens, phone numbers, or Messaging Service SIDs. All credentials come from Doppler.
- NEVER send SMS without routing through the Sovereign SMS Router intent classifier. Direct `twilio.messages.create()` calls from routes are forbidden.
- NEVER change the 6-pipe intent enum: `PLATFORM_OTP | PLATFORM_CARE | PLATFORM_MKTG | CUSTOMER_OTP | CUSTOMER_CARE | CUSTOMER_MKTG`. These map to registered A2P campaigns.
- NEVER disable or stub out opt-out handling. STOP keyword compliance is a legal requirement.
- NEVER send outbound SMS to a number in `sms_opt_outs` without re-consent.

## If You Need to Add a New SMS Use Case

Route it through the SMS Router. Classify the intent. Do not create a new send path outside the router. Adding a new pipe requires A2P campaign registration — open a compliance task first.
